{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530050-the-boogeyman-a-bane-idea","id":1530050,"title":"The Boogeyman: A Bane Idea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-05T13:28:06-08:00","id":1530050,"title":"The Boogeyman: A Bane Idea","content":"I came up with a very interesting Bane Idea and I would like some advice on making it work in Werewolf, either W:20 Canon or W: 5<br /> <br /> My idea so far is a Bane that models itself after the Boogeyman and feeds off the fears it generates from the Children it torments in the night, especially delighting in their screams of fear.<br /> <br /> Like Pennywise, the creature is a very capable shapeshifter, able to generate any form, especially forms that reflect a child's worst fear. However, it's favorite form to take is corrupted and twisted versions of the war forms of the various Changing Breeds, taking delight in the terror the infamous Crinos form gives it's young victims.<br /> <br /> This idea is either for a campaign or a piece of fiction and I would like help molding this idea into something that fits nicely with Werewolf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T15:24:03-08:00","id":1530056,"title":"","content":"It's a solid idea although a Bane would probably want to do more than just scare children. It should probably be something that kills children. Either the child disappears (like the victims of Pennywise) after being killed and eaten, or the child is found dead in its bed for inexplicable reasons. That doesn't mean it has to kill all the time, or that it won't engage in a prolonged campaign to generate fear in children before it decides to kill. But to make it a good foe for the Garou, I think the life of children will need to be at stake.<br /> <br /> There are all sorts of boogeymen found in world cultures, so making it a shapechanging Bane that can assume a variety of forms allows you to use the same Bane regardless of the specifics of the form a specific child sees.<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that until the last few centuries, many adults also believed in fearsome creatures that could do them harm. These were less likely to be inside the house, but instead dwell in dangerous places in the wilderness and at night. Cautionary tales in a time when being stuck outside at night could be very dangerous. So think whether you want something more general that plagues mankind, or something that specifically targets children (if so, when does it stop threatening the child - when he reaches puberty?). Also think of how this Bane would act and be treated throughout all the ages - not just for modern time in developed nations, but going back through the ages even the Stone Age when humanity was migrating hunter-gatherers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T17:50:33-08:00","id":1530061,"title":"","content":"Following up on what Black Fox said, you could have Bane attack children, but be smart enough to follow orders and also attack adults, even if they aren't his favorite prey. So any formori could use it to attack opponents, like a police officer who asks too many questions, a reporter who sticks her nose where it shouldn't, the leader of a union, activist group or representative of a community, like &quot;you do what I say and the nightmares stop&quot; and he won't be able to ask for help because, you know, no proof, it's worse if he has children so he can use them as hostages.<br /> <br /> Now moving on to the M.O., and I apologize if this seems too cruel, he could attack children through nightmares making them feel afraid, but not their greatest fears, the bogeyman would attack, making the child develop new traumas instead of recycling the old ones, like she suddenly becomes afraid of something she liked, stops trusting people for fear, getting close to animals that could hurt her, going to other places with hidden dangers, she will see danger in everything and everyone, added to sleep deprivation, this little by little undermines her psychologically and weakens her mind, so she can become a receptacle for other Banes in the future, you know, that phrase that says &quot;weak mind is the devil's workshop&quot;, or just become an adult without any attitude and therefore meek and obedient.<br /> <br /> Another way of using this is that the bogeyman would seek to undermine a child mentally so that he can use him as a vessel in the physical world by possessing him, once in this state he could cause nightmares, even with the victim being awake and since he possesses the body of a child that would make even the Garou hesitate. If you really insist on shapeshifting abilities, an almost as good option would be that the bogeyman could cause hallucinations so strong that they would have real consequences for the body, they would still be illusions, but the fire still burns, blades still cut, poison still intoxicate (although in the latter it stops when the illusion ends.) it's just an idea to maintain the classic bogeyman concept.<br /> <br /> One idea I had while writing was that he could hunt children and grandchildren of Garous in order to cause them a lot of stress and induce a first change in childhood, but the human body would not yet be ready for the changes which results in child's death, I think it would be good way to make the Garou feel a sense of urgency with this Bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}